From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:40:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-msm8953: enable USB FSM parent for clock
 operations

The USB master branch needs the PCNOC USB AXI branch running for its FSM
to complete a transition. The existing parent workaround orders normal
consumer enable/disable operations, but unused-clock cleanup invokes
the branch operation without enabling an otherwise-unused parent.
This leaves the bootloader-enabled master branch unable to halt.

Use CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE so the common clock framework temporarily
enables the FSM dependency during unused-clock cleanup and other clock
operations. Preserve normal clock gating and the existing halt checks;
do not mark the clock critical or ignore unused clocks.

Origin: Local ThinkSmart View port
Source: https://github.com/msm8953-mainline/linux
Base-commit: 755ffc44d5d8442adeec8bbaa02108478089c4d7

---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8953.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8953.c
index c4ec9950ab683f96962392b5a11f8d3b9f54abd1..d417fa4b6c91f0a05ef2997d491df8341ce8c9af 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8953.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-msm8953.c
@@ -3651,7 +3651,7 @@ static struct clk_branch gcc_usb30_master_clk = {
 			},
 			.num_parents = 1,
 			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
-			.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
+			.flags = CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT | CLK_OPS_PARENT_ENABLE,
 		}
 	}
 };
